{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense","id":415848,"title":"Dragon Blooded Defense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-22T16:59:34-08:00","id":415848,"title":"Dragon Blooded Defense","content":"I have some high end lunars and Solars that are about to face the Realms Dragon Blooded legions. How do I make them scary? The Lunars and Solars are kicking around high 30's dice pools on average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:05:50-08:00","id":415886,"title":"","content":"Not much you can do other than maybe some Sidereal Support and a few Elder Exalts. DB's can be scary, but unless you have a lot of highly competent ones they aren't really High End Celestial Scary.<br /> <br /> You might get some value out of using everything in Thousand Correct Actions to your advantage by forcing things to be mass combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:08:38-08:00","id":415889,"title":"","content":"Onslaught penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:09:57-08:00","id":415890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=415886#post415886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much you can do other than maybe some Sidereal Support and a few Elder Exalts. DB's can be scary, but unless you have a lot of highly competent ones they aren't really High End Celestial Scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some things you can do, depending on what the PCs are up to with their charms. Coordinated attacks can be scary, if your target doesn't have a DV penalty negator. If they've got that and Infinite Ability Mastery or such the like, there's really nothing you can do, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T17:56:57-08:00","id":415933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=415886#post415886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might get some value out of using everything in Thousand Correct Actions to your advantage by forcing things to be mass combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this. Mass Combat is not a system really anybody wants to use, and making Dragon-Bloods a combat threat at the high-end generally involves armies. It's, well, in their blood.<br /> <br /> That being said, how many of them are immune to environmental penalties and environmental damage? It doesn't matter how many dice you're rolling for defense, if you stand in the middle of a Dragon-Blood created volcano, <i>you get hit</i>. (Meanwhile Dragon-Bloods can rather trivially immunize themselves and their followers from their own firepower.) Making heavy use of Dragon Vortex Attack and Dragon-Seared Battlefield can go a long way to making a legion of DBs as terrifying as it should be. Getting to shape and direct those via the charm from TCA helps a lot as well, and one of the maneuvers in TCA is getting to turn a Dragon Vortex into a true perfect defense.<br /> <br /> On a personal level, Surging (Ability) Mastery lets dragon-bloods get close to Celestial dice pools for a while, but they run out of motes and willpower before too long. In that time, however, they can do a lot of damage. TCA charms let you bless all your buddies for a whole scene with all the Dragon-Graced Weapon you know, and if you know all of them, hitting somebody knocks them down, poisons them, delays and penalizes their next action, and does a bunch of damage. It's not quite on the level of Solar &quot;I hit him and he evaporates&quot; but it can get pretty scary.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods can also have &quot;tanks&quot; at high end, with a combination of taunting ability and eventually the power to link minds to reflexively defend everyone else who is part of the group mind (one of the ultimate powers that Celestials want for their DB allies, since there's nothing on the Celestial end that can replicate it).<br /> <br /> Celestial Martial Arts (especially Crane Style) helps DBs punch above their weight class as well, Ragara Myrrun knows a bunch of heretical styles in addition to the immaculate ones so if the DBs are pulling out all the stops to stomp on the biggest eminent threat to the Realm, expect more breadth of expertise than your average war party.<br /> <br /> Finally, Sidereals are pretty good at helping, whether it's through astrological blessings or Throne Shadow Style or being far better informed than anyone else or just straight-up shanking a bitch, so depending on how high-end we're talking it's not at all weird to see them participate. If they've got a good exit strategy you could see high-end Bronzies with Scarlet Patterned Battlefield Style making real trouble when in conjunction with DB armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 02-22-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:01:09-08:00","id":416036,"title":"","content":"Wait for Ex3. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:03:34-08:00","id":416038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416036#post416036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait for Ex3. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar players are gonna be waiting a couple more years to upgrade in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T20:15:09-08:00","id":416040,"title":"","content":"Everyone has mentioned taking it to Mass Combat already. That's one of three prongs of the Realm's approach to the threat of a whole mess of high-end Anathema.<br /> <br /> The second prong? Gear.<br /> <br /> The Realm is not going to send <i>just</i> a bunch of guys in armor wielding daiklave's against a full cadre of Anathema working together unless it has no other choice. They're going to break out the artifacts. We're talking <i>multiple</i> guys in Warstriders. We're talking Dragon Armor. (It's not just for Lookshy.) We're talking every weird piece of first age weaponry they dredge out of their armories that looks like it might be useful.<br /> <br /> The third prong? Immaculates.<br /> <br /> This is what a non-trivial part of the Immaculate Order has spent their whole lives training for. We're talking multiple Immaculate MA masters, who also have Defense-From-Anathema Method. We're talking probably a Grandmaster. (There are a couple more of them than just Myrrun.)<br /> <br /> Aside from that, if the Realm is marching openly against a bunch of high-end Celestials you guys are probably viewed as an existential threat to the Realm. So plan accordingly. I am going to assume that someone who actually knows what the hell they are doing is calling the shots for the Realm at the highest levels, like Cathak Cainan, Sesus Nagezzar, or the Roseblack. The Realm can transform from a giant inefficient slug to a terrifying engine of extinction very quickly when it has to, and it isn't above doing things like &quot;Okay, we're going to abandon An-Teng, because we need the legions elsewhere. Yes, we're going to abandon ALL of it. We can take it back later.&quot; The Realm is going to dig deep. Ask yourself what the Realm could possibly have on tap for just this scenario and then deploy it.<br /> <br /> A bunch of people have already mentioned the Siddies. I would be real, real hesitant about suddenly busting them out if they haven't been a presence thus far. Would they get involved? Absolutely. But it has to be handled with care. Your players might or might not resent the reality ninjas suddenly busting in out of nowhere to save the Realm's bacon. If Sidereals haven't been a presence in your game so far at all AND your PCs haven't done anything the Gold Faction finds objectionable, I would recommend hand-waving things as &quot;the Bronze Faction did their voodoo, and then the Gold Faction did their hoodoo, and it all cancelled out.&quot;<br /> <br /> A note of warning: be prepared for your PCs to disengage. You probably know them better than we do. But sometimes groups of players look at the business end of a Realm hammer and go &quot;Nope. Nope nope nope nope. Could we win? Yeah, probably. But I'm not wading into THAT unless I absolutely have to. I'm going to fade back into the jungle/forest/steppe/etc. and let them run around exhausting themselves, spending ruinous sums of money maintaining that expeditionary force, and killing every Wyld Hunt they detach from the main force to try and smoke me out. Eventually they'll either fall apart at the seams or go home, and I'll strike THEN.&quot;<br /> <br /> It can happen. Have a Plan B.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:11:03-08:00","id":416117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=415889#post415889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onslaught penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars and Lunars with 30 dice on their combat actions? They're not going to be affected by onslaught penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:30:31-08:00","id":416168,"title":"","content":"Also? Turns out hundreds of Dragonbloods combined probably have more motes than you, and they know your motes run out.<br /> <br /> Expect a first-wave of expendable cannon fodder, a second wave of badasses who are also cannon fodder to make you waste most of your energy, and then a third wave with the Big Guns.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:17:30-08:00","id":416209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416168#post416168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also? Turns out hundreds of Dragonbloods combined probably have more motes than you, and they know your motes run out.<br /> <br /> Expect a first-wave of expendable cannon fodder, a second wave of badasses who are also cannon fodder to make you waste most of your energy, and then a third wave with the Big Guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may backfire on the Realm, as if these guys are sufficiently badass Celestials they'll have access to scenelength charms that let them shred basically unlimited numbers of cannon fodder for a very reasonable mote cost, but yeah, that too. The Dragon-Blooded have religious and cultural imperatives telling them that it is sweet and honorable to die on the end of an Anathema's blade if it lets the Dragon-Blooded <i>behind</i> them clamber over the corpse and lop the filthy hellspawns head off.<br /> <br /> Savare was slightly light on the details, though. I mean, a lot of little variables can change this, do the PCs have their own armies to soak up the non-Exalted parts of the Legions, are the Sidereals an active force in this game, is the Realm being run by someone who is both competent and selfless, just competent but not selfless, or neither? Those things matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:28:47-08:00","id":416252,"title":"","content":"Dragon bloods have access to some of the most powerful artifacts remaining in Creation. Remember that and make use of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:49:57-08:00","id":416262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416040#post416040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone has mentioned taking it to Mass Combat already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:09:48-08:00","id":416277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416262#post416262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sure didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess you're not included in everyone then. Welcome back to 4th grade PE class where everyone forgets you exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:29:23-08:00","id":416289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416040#post416040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second prong? Gear.<br /> <br /> The Realm is not going to send <i>just</i> a bunch of guys in armor wielding daiklave's against a full cadre of Anathema working together unless it has no other choice. They're going to break out the artifacts. We're talking <i>multiple</i> guys in Warstriders. We're talking Dragon Armor. (It's not just for Lookshy.) We're talking every weird piece of first age weaponry they dredge out of their armories that looks like it might be useful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>something like the eye of the fire dragon maybe? and lets not forget the perfected kata bracers. now slap that on a essence five fire aspect with &quot;defense from anathema method&quot; and even a dawn will be feeling that sting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:41:32-08:00","id":416293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416289#post416289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something like the eye of the fire dragon maybe? and lets not forget the perfected kata bracers. now slap that on a essence five fire aspect with &amp;quot;defense from anathema method&amp;quot; and even a dawn will be feeling that sting</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's only one of the former in all Creation, and the later is a kind of broken artifact. Although at least, I think, if the PCs get their hands on it they won't be able to effectively use it without a harmonic adaptor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T02:11:18-08:00","id":416304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416289#post416289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something like the eye of the fire dragon maybe? and lets not forget the perfected kata bracers. now slap that on a essence five fire aspect with &amp;quot;defense from anathema method&amp;quot; and even a dawn will be feeling that sting</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that an entire fang of Terrestrials armed with Plasma Tongue Repeaters and profecient with Archery Charms would be very difficult for a group of Celestial Exalts to avoid without activating scene long defenses. each Talon would be led by an Immaculate learned in Righteous Devil Style.<br /> <br /> And thats just for starters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T02:26:06-08:00","id":416308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416304#post416304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would imagine that an entire fang of Terrestrials armed with Plasma Tongue Repeaters and profecient with Archery Charms would be very difficult for a group of Celestial Exalts to avoid without activating scene long defenses. each Talon would be led by an Immaculate learned in Righteous Devil Style.<br /> <br /> And thats just for starters...</div> </div> </div> </div>how about a bunch of earth dragon style martial artists that just focus on trying to &quot;weapon breaking defense&quot; their artifacts from them as a first wave? followed by the plasma tongues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:41:07-08:00","id":416414,"title":"","content":"Would hit and run work? Attack them make them commit their scene longs (IAM + Flow Like Blood etc..) then disengage, attack the next scene w/o letting them recover much of the motes spent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T05:45:07-08:00","id":416418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416304#post416304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine that an entire fang of Terrestrials armed with Plasma Tongue Repeaters and profecient with Archery Charms\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>DB Archery Charms are specifically only compatible with bows. No ballista Earth Aspect, and no barrage of PTR Fire Aspects. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2026each Talon would be led by an Immaculate learned in Righteous Devil Style. </div> </div> </div>You mean the style they don't learn and in fact treat as heretical? Sure, let's get right on that\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thats just for starters... </div> </div> </div>I think we're after finishers, here\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416414#post416414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would hit and run work? Attack them make them commit their scene longs (IAM + Flow Like Blood etc..) then disengage, attack the next scene w/o letting them recover much of the motes spent?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want them to torch their motes, you want to get 'em with Essence-Disrupting Attack - if even one of them didn't spring for IPP in their mad rush to get their insane dice pools, it's worth the cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-23-2015, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T06:45:25-08:00","id":416444,"title":"","content":"Just a minor addition to what others have said. Enfolded in the Dragon's Wings allows a DB commander to protect his entire legion from the effects on his/her anima and from attacks like dragon vortex. So if a wing of troops is walking towards your anathema, with their commander gained lots of bonus successes for free because of their army at their back while sitting in the middle of a giant flame tornado that moves with his unit and is directed by a special character other DB in the unit, well, then you have something that looks pretty threatening even if your Celestials will triumph. That is just two Dragon Bloods and some mortals, now if you have two sworn brotherhoods you can have five units like that. Also if you are using an honest to god legion their are at least 5 dragons of troops at their disposal which can add tons of successes in mass combat.<br /> <br /> I know people poo poo mass combat, but if you ignore endurance (which in my experience battles don't last long enough, or your players get bored, before it becomes a factor) and do a little prep it just becomes a wad of free successes for your dragonbloods.<br /> <br /> Not to mention DBs get a perfect defense when leading a mass combat unit with their upgrade to portentous comet deflecting mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be more Zen","edited":{"userid":3985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3985-daedalus","user":"Daedalus","date":".  Forgot the perfect 02-23-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3985-daedalus","name":"Daedalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:29:30-08:00","id":416507,"title":"","content":"None of the above would work against competent high end Solars.<br /> <br /> I can give you idea about high end DB builds but you have to be more specific about errata version and houserules used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:52:39-08:00","id":416526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416418#post416418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DB Archery Charms are specifically only compatible with bows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been torn on how to treat that fact.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I've always figured &quot;the Realm can't be that dumb, there have got to be a number of specialists who have custom-cut Archery charms designed to work with things other than powerbows.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then on the other hand I think &quot;no, they really can be that dumb, can't they? They treat the bowmen/slingers in their Legions like shit, explicitly paying them less and equipping them worse than anyone else, and there's an immense cultural bias towards melee weapons in the Realm. They may, in fact, not have anyone specifically trained to apply their archery charms to anything but a powerbow. Such people probably exist, I'm sure there's that one weird Dynast who was stationed in Chairoscuro and developed an intense love for his pair of plasma tongue repeaters and has adapted a ton of Archery charms just for them and walks around strapped all the time in a duster coat and doesn't get invited to the good parties. But it won't be official policy or anything.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:00:12-08:00","id":416529,"title":"","content":"Move the confrontation to the sea. Leader keywords really really wreck when the entire crew is basically using them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:45:22-08:00","id":416643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416418#post416418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DB Archery Charms are specifically only compatible with bows. No ballista Earth Aspect, and no barrage of PTR Fire Aspects. <br /> <br /> If you want them to torch their motes, you want to get 'em with Essence-Disrupting Attack - if even one of them didn't spring for IPP in their mad rush to get their insane dice pools, it's worth the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check page 48 of the errata for &quot;beyond bows&quot; for wood aspects with ironwood flame weapons.<br /> <br /> Also IPP lasts a full day, everyone who has it uses it before they go to bed each night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:23:26-08:00","id":416696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Savare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense#post415848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some high end lunars and Solars that are about to face the Realms Dragon Blooded legions. How do I make them scary? The Lunars and Solars are kicking around high 30's dice pools on average.</div> </div> </div> </div>A better question to ask is why would the Terrestrials would agree to fight a battle that is so heavily against them?<br /> <br /> To make the Terrestrials a functional threat, stop thinking of them as mooks and start thinking of them as players fighting a superior foe. No starting character solar will willingly stand their ground when a group of deathlords show up.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Read Sun Tzu's the Art of War<br /> <br /> Step 2: Avoid direct combat with the Celestials at all costs unless you can catch them alone with nearly overwhelming numbers and fire power.<br /> <br /> Step 3: Make the Celestials constantly choose between goals. They can attack the Blessed Isle or they can abandon the attack to counter an attack on their supply lines. If they attack the Realm, they may take ground but they will lose resources and allies. If they route the terrestrial preemptive strike, they lose the momentum to attack the Blessed Isle for a while longer, thus giving the Terrestrials a chance to make more plans and set up better defenses.<br /> <br /> Step 4: A Terrestrial legion of 5,000 soldiers can hit multiple targets at the same time. Unless the Celestials have spent a great deal of time setting up teleportation infrastructure to get from place to place quickly, there are just not enough Celestials to fight all the battles at once.<br /> <br /> Thus the way to win or at least provide a challenge with Terrestrials is to think along the lines of having the Celestials win individual battles but lose the war.<br /> <br /> Or if you are dead set on having the Terrestrials be suicidal, remember that Summon Elemental doesn't have a limitation on power level, just summon a half dozen lesser elemental dragons to bolster the strength of the legions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:36:34-08:00","id":416703,"title":"","content":"Just for clarity, the circle is playing through the Return of the Scarlet Empress story line. And right now the Ebon Dragon has been freed. The Solars have gathered an army of their own and are now on the march to defeat those forces. This is some impressive responses. I will have to look into all your suggestions. Because going up against them one on one isn't working. And I cant say that an Infernal commander commands every army. And the Lunar is about to get put into his own Jade Prison. He took Moonsilver Absorption. So now he truly is a Juggernaught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:37:18-08:00","id":416704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416696#post416696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A better question to ask is why would the Terrestrials would agree to fight a battle that is so heavily against them?<br /> <br /> To make the Terrestrials a functional threat, stop thinking of them as mooks and start thinking of them as players fighting a superior foe. No starting character solar will willingly stand their ground when a group of deathlords show up.<br /> <br /> Step 1: Read Sun Tzu's the Art of War<br /> <br /> Step 2: Avoid direct combat with the Celestials at all costs unless you can catch them alone with nearly overwhelming numbers and fire power.<br /> <br /> Step 3: Make the Celestials constantly choose between goals. They can attack the Blessed Isle or they can abandon the attack to counter an attack on their supply lines. If they attack the Realm, they may take ground but they will lose resources and allies. If they route the terrestrial preemptive strike, they lose the momentum to attack the Blessed Isle for a while longer, thus giving the Terrestrials a chance to make more plans and set up better defenses.<br /> <br /> Step 4: A Terrestrial legion of 5,000 soldiers can hit multiple targets at the same time. Unless the Celestials have spent a great deal of time setting up teleportation infrastructure to get from place to place quickly, there are just not enough Celestials to fight all the battles at once.<br /> <br /> Thus the way to win or at least provide a challenge with Terrestrials is to think along the lines of having the Celestials win individual battles but lose the war.<br /> <br /> Or if you are dead set on having the Terrestrials be suicidal, remember that Summon Elemental doesn't have a limitation on power level, just summon a half dozen lesser elemental dragons to bolster the strength of the legions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right, I need to start thinking beyond the scale of a single battle. Play this more like Risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:39:34-08:00","id":416705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416696#post416696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A better question to ask is why would the Terrestrials would agree to fight a battle that is so heavily against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's really not a better way to kill Celestials. Really, there isn't. The Usurpation involved complete and utter tactical and strategic surprise coupled with massive Sidereal involvement and the Dragon-Blooded still died in droves. The only way to kill a Celestial Exalt who has had time to grow powerful is with another Celestial Exalt or throwing wave after wave after wave of Terrestrials at them.<br /> <br /> I think the analogy once made was that it's the difference between fighting 100 ants and 100 cats. You can't just SMOOSH the cats, so eventually they're probably going to win.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, your ideas are good ones, and any smart Dragon-Blooded leader is going to use all of them, but eventually you're going to need to get down to brass tacks, and that's going to involve smashing your legion into the Celestials headlong and hoping that they're the ones who break rather than you. Ideally, this will happen in a situation where they have a massive strategic and tactical advantage, but perfect hits don't come along every day and eventually you'll have to make some kind of call along the lines of &quot;we know they're down some unspecified number of motes and their allies aren't all with them, this is as good as it will probably ever get, go time is now.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T12:05:15-08:00","id":416735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416705#post416705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there's really not a better way to kill Celestials. Really, there isn't. The Usurpation involved complete and utter tactical and strategic surprise coupled with massive Sidereal involvement and the Dragon-Blooded still died in droves. The only way to kill a Celestial Exalt who has had time to grow powerful is with another Celestial Exalt or throwing wave after wave after wave of Terrestrials at them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Usurpation doesn't matter. It's a fiat event. It's not supported by the mechanics of Exalted and STs have nothing to learn from it about the mechanics of Celestials vs DBs battles.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely must model the Usurpation with 2/2.5 mechanics, your best bet is vaguely fiat-ing that the Sidereals have dodged the Solar Investigation charms that predict future danger, then somehow boosted a manse temporarily to N/A, used geomancy to snuff Solar Circle Magic and the Greater Sign of Venus to snuff Charms (obviously from Prismatic Arrangement &quot;I act first on tick 0&quot;, and then unleashed the DB hordes on the Solars.<br /> <br /> Even so, any Solar with the same SMA, or Awareness perfect charms like the Spirit one, or simply custom Solar charms (we're talking dozens if not hundreds of Elder Solars here) for perfectly acting on tick 0 will activate reflexive teleports of various sorcery/artifact/charm/or-even-wyld-stunt stripes, port to their inassailable fortresses in the corners of Creation and the Wyld, summon the Third Circles, Wyld Shape a greater army than the DBs could ever hope to be, and crush this little Usurpation (again, the Sids might have a slim chance to stop them, the DBs are a nonentity in this contest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:04:15-08:00","id":416948,"title":"","content":"Sure, you can absolutely make Dragon-Bloods threatening. You don't even need to use martial arts to do it, though it helps.<br /> <br /> First, make sure you have a good grasp of their excellencies. With an applicable speciality, Speciality Focus and the First and Second excellencies, they add four dice and two successes for three motes, or one success for free. Optimized for dodge and with hearthstone bracers, an E5 DB has a DDV of 12 without spending a mote.<br /> <br /> Second, Defence From Anathema Method is a must. It has fewer prerequisites after errata, and all of them are pretty good, including the DB Shaping defence and perfect social defence. For 5m, 1wp, DfAM maxes out your DVs and MDVs for the scene whenever you are near Celestials. Passive DDV can raise to 15 for the scene.<br /> <br /> Third, External Penalties. With Thrown you have Elemental Armor Technique, which, when repurchased for the Earth and Fire versions, allows a scene long -3 external penalty against all attacks. Whirlwind Shield increases that by 3 against range. Over in Dodge, Elemental Defence Technique can inflict a further -2 penalty, but cannot be repurchased to select the effect, so it depends upon aspect.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the vortex. Dragon Vortex Attack is formidable on its own, but as an elemental hazard its penalties and damage can be resisted by Celestial Charms. However, upgraded with Wrath Directing Gesture, it can be used as a perfect defence for the whole group. Using the Sculpt and Shield functions, it can be reshaped reflexively to defend any ally within its radius for 11m. Provided Dragon-Bloods are flaring their animas (and of course they are) they are immune to the damage inflicted by this method of defence, so the only downside is that the Vortex itself is expensive to establish for the scene; 15m, 1wp.<br /> <br /> Fifth, Immaculate martial arts are formidable, but don't overlook the utility of Terrestrial Melee in offense. With full repurchases of Dragon-Graced Weapon and Dragon Blade Beneficence, the entire party can do a host of badtouch supplemental effects for free. Better yet, if you are fighting those pesky Infernals or Abyssals, everyone's damage becomes aggravated. If your opponent is unwise enough to neglect tick-long or longer penalty negation, a group attack enhanced by Threshing Floor Technique will rapidly drive their DVs into the ground.<br /> <br /> Sixth, With One Mind allows the group to reflexively Defend Other each member. A couple of members specced for high Parry DV and the Conflagration of Warding offer an additional layer of defence.<br /> <br /> Finally, cooperative Elemental Bolt is not to be underestimated. Combine a 50+ damage 30 attack dice death-sphere and have your Thrown specialist continue to use it every round for one mote a pop!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416735#post416735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the DBs are a nonentity in this contest</div> </div> </div> </div>Your move, mister Streak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 02-23-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T17:48:34-08:00","id":417009,"title":"","content":"Congratulations, you've demonstrated a method by which a group of DBs might survive for a few actions worth of combat before mote taping against advanced Celestials and at the same time put a small amount of stress on a Celestials Mote pool. Give me about 10 full Sworn Brotherhoods of Elders build exactly this way and you might be on you way to killing one of the Celestials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:47:37-08:00","id":417091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416948#post416948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your move, mister Streak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh? You're presently 1/3 way in piling external/internal penalties compared to the post about the importance of penalties for DBs I made on the old forum. So to say, you're on the right path as penalties are uncapped unlike the pitiful Charm caps of the DBs, but there's more to it. Mind you, this way might produce antagonists challenging to the OP's party, but it cannot by itself challenge actual high XP/backgrounds Essence 5+ Solars who are competently built. Such characters exist on a higher level in both pure power and, even more importantly, versatility and control.<br /> <br /> As I cannot link the old forum (archivation failed) I can instead remind you of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/280072-why-do-you-like-dragon-blooded/page3\">this thread about Dragonblooded</a> where we discussed Dragonblooded disfunction in 2/2.5 both in fluff and crunch. There I posted two characters I have used as Elder &quot;DB&quot; challenges to Celestial parties.<br /> <br /> The first one was from early in the edition, probably just after Scroll of Heroes and prior to the Dawn Solution or even splats like Oadenol's. So in the time of Core-perfects only, no tick/action-longs, and we as always used stunts in the way that eventually became the codified one: one per action, not one per attack/defense as the Chungians advocated which made the Solars even more ridiculous. So that character, an Earth Master/Hill-Crushing Hero mix, had accuracy and soak in the 80s, damage in the 60s, PDV of 30 or so, was facing relatively low-xp Solars who lacked plenty of powerful options even for the limited amount of splatbooks at the time...and was defeated. <br /> <br /> The other character is from the late 2.0 edition, is akuma/DB (so probably OK for the RotSE but you can drop the akuma stuff and focus on the DB goodies if you will). Just some of the things she had included:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mantle of Elemental Fusion, fused with a Lesser Earth Dragon of the Quicksilver Queen stature. The main benefits derived are Essence Plethoras, Destiny Sponsorship inflicted 15 external penalty on attacks against Dodge DV, Invincible Symbol of Authority:Earth that denies/reduces earth and metal based attacks, including magic materials based on metals.<br /> <br /> - Transcendant Gaian Harmony:Air and Wood, inflicting 8 to 16 external penalties on certain attacks per the animas (She's Earth Aspect)<br /> <br /> - lesser penalty applicators like Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon and Flowing Water Defense (note that her stats presume a fight going on for some time so she has accumulated enough Water Style free motes)<br /> <br /> - Unchain the Dragon's Heart: probably won't come into play, but if it does it's a nasty surprise<br /> <br /> - Ordained Talons of Draconic Fury on the Eye of the Fire Dragon. That's the Rate 13 weapon line and the artifact itself does aggravated damage and charmbreaks Solars </div> </div> </div>So, those who could at all engage her through her exceptional stealth/mobility were to face near full immunity to damage from magical materials (and a ward against Solar charm-magic weapons), DVs and penalties combining in the 50-100 range, the &quot;best&quot; of Cobra and Water Dragon and Joy in Adversity mote economy, high rate, high accuracy, aggravated charm-breaking attacks...and did she win against competent established Solars of just 5 Essence? No, she didn't. So the maximum system juice for Dragonblooded couldn't deal with Solars half-way to Essence 10, even when the Solars chose to engage instead of evading and annihilating everything Dragonblooded through Sorcery, Wyld Shaping, and minion-boosting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:53:04-08:00","id":417099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417009#post417009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations, you've demonstrated a method by which a group of DBs might survive for a few actions worth of combat before mote taping against advanced Celestials and at the same time put a small amount of stress on a Celestials Mote pool. Give me about 10 full Sworn Brotherhoods of Elders build exactly this way and you might be on you way to killing one of the Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on what charms those Solars are packing, yeah this is pretty much true. There's a lot of BS at higher essence, and if you're talking about charms like the Solar version of Ordained Talon of Draconic Fury, then definitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T20:34:24-08:00","id":417136,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of using Ramparts of Obedient Earth to stage a trap. Have several essence 4+ Earth Aspects lay in wait underground and have them suddenly reshape the earth everyone's on into a giant death trap. I think the errata says that at Essence 4, each one can shape Essence x 10 cubic yards per activation. So alot of them could make it where someone using monkey leap wouldn't be able to clear the trap.<br /> <br /> Also remember, what's good for goose is good for the gander. If your players are using weird math and stacking artifact bonuses to get their high 30's dice pools, then a high essence DB should be able to use the same tricks (as long as it's not the result of Solar/Lunar charms).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I know alot of people have suggested using mass combat already. It's a good idea. If you want to avoid Mass Combat then you're really handicapping your DBs. You might consider some custom powers to the DB's in order to make up for the loss of the combat system that they excel at.<br /> <br /> Additionally, remember that with alot of soldiers in the mix, alot of DB's will have several guards doing protect other actions and blockade movement actions.<br /> <br /> Finally, it's probably a good idea for any combat to start with the DB's anticipating it and having their defenses up already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 02-23-2015, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T21:54:00-08:00","id":417192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416705#post416705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the analogy once made was that it's the difference between fighting 100 ants and 100 cats. You can't just SMOOSH the cats, so eventually they're probably going to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that the ants probably have a better chance at doing major damage. Kick over a bullet ant nest and they swarm you, they are small enough not to be noticed and can get inside your defenses. <br /> <br /> Getting back to the matter at hand, there is a critical concept to understand, unless the ST and Players have agreed to play this sort of game, there is little chance of the Celestials being killed. Obviously there is always a chance that the player does something stupid and the dice fail them at ta critical moment, but it is unlikely. The terrestrials on the other hand are expected to die.<br /> <br /> People talk about Celestial mote pool advantage all the time, but I rarely hear about anyone bringing out a couple dozen Terrestrials in Wood Dragon armor and laying down a mote suppression field so severe that nearly all essence use is brought to a halt, which when you think about it means there is remarkably little dice difference between the Celestials and the run of the mill mortal legion soldiers.<br /> <br /> Hell you could make an argument that the Empress had a plan for Celestials attacking the Blessed Isle since she is a shogunate era officer with a very clear understanding of what Celestial Exalts are. Imagine if the Terrestrials and the Sidereals built stand alone devices to generate the Wood Dragon Armor field, considering that they were integrated into the armor they would be simple to make as stand alones. Of course I would do something evil like upgrade them so they are more powerful. They could have been sitting in an imperial armory for centuries just waiting for this day to come.<br /> <br /> I guess it is like playing Evolve, the terrestrials are the hunters and the Celestials are similar to (or in the case of Lunars actually are) the monster. You win by team work, as opposed to just throwing massed numbers at the enemy.<br /> <br /> Imagine setting wood dragon armor devices up to create a nullification arena, then you send the mortal troops in to it to fight the Celestial. While that is happening the Terrestrials and perhaps the random Sidereal are making sniper shots from outside the field when an opportunity presents itself. Or they could soften up the Celestial before sending in the mortals by using artillery of some type to deplete what few uses of defensive charms they could have.<br /> <br /> That would be a starting point, next you start asking yourself about the war manses that dot the landscape of the Blessed Isle. They power the Imperial Defense Grid, but if you consider the fact that you still have points left over after all the Relays, you can still have a functional manse. So what sort of battlefield applications could these manses have? Integrated Greater Elemental Lens from the Dragonfly boat that allows Terrestrial attack charms to be absolutely terrifying makes for one hell of a artillery piece.<br /> <br /> Alternatively the manse could have been designed as an aid station to heal wounded and depleted soldiers. With the right integrated artifacts and manse powers a terrestrial can be fully healed and completely mote recharged within moments of entering the manse. This means that your Terrestrials can tag team the Celestials by swapping out before they get mote tapped or too badly damaged.<br /> <br /> Of course I would do things like rig the manse with mote recharge and the Greater Elemental Lens so the Terrestrials never run out of juice.<br /> <br /> So I would suggest thinking along the lines of how to make the Celestials fight at a disadvantage at every turn.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:54:31-08:00","id":417346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416643#post416643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also IPP lasts a full day, everyone who has it uses it before they go to bed each night.</div> </div> </div> </div>People gotta quit with these fuckin' absolutes - <i>I've played a character that didn't</i>. He only kicked it off when he had to - i.e., in response to Shaping attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T02:45:40-08:00","id":417382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=416705#post416705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there's really not a better way to kill Celestials. Really, there isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is.Get a bunch of soldiers. Make sure everytime that celestial turns his back to you, they get attacked. They go to sleep? Burn the house they are sleeping in down. Try to eat something? Make sure it is poisoned. They charge at you? Wait for them to blow up their full set of combat charms, then disengage. Attack their allies, bases, troops when celestials are otherwise occupied. Rinse and repeat until they are worn down enough that you can make a finishing kill.<br /> <br /> Still, there are some high-essence builds that are ridiculously overpowered even in 2.5e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:24:34-08:00","id":417400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417009#post417009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations, you've demonstrated a method by which a group of DBs might survive for a few actions worth of combat before mote taping against advanced Celestials and at the same time put a small amount of stress on a Celestials Mote pool. Give me about 10 full Sworn Brotherhoods of Elders build exactly this way and you might be on you way to killing one of the Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confident that Dragon-Bloods of equal Essence and experience can take Solars at a five to one ratio.<br /> <br /> No cheese, no broken artifacts, no &quot;creative&quot; rule interpretations, Akuma bullshit, mutations, merits, whatever. Even in a fight under rules and conditions a sane storyteller would allow, Terrestrials can absolutely win.<br /> <br /> DBs can get a good passive DV+External penalty using the Charms stated above, with no need to spent motes per dodge. This is enough to counter most attacks enhanced with only IAM. In the face of a undodgeable or penalty negating attack, they can group PD using Dragon Vortex or Defend Other PD using Conflagration of Warding. The group's collective stunt recovery will be enough to cover their defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 02-24-2015, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:30:35-08:00","id":417403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417400#post417400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am confident that Dragon-Bloods of equal Essence and experience can take Solars of equal Essence at a five to one ratio. No cheese, no broken artifacts, no &quot;creative&quot; rule interpretations, Akuma bullshit, mutations, merits, whatever. Even in a fight under rules and conditions a sane storyteller would allow, Terrestrials can absolutely win.</div> </div> </div> </div>how about safety among enemies i mean the Celestials are going to miss sometime so why not make that miss into something that might hit another celestial with that automatic counter attack charm. make them Demetheus their allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:39:06-08:00","id":417406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417403#post417403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how about safety among enemies i mean the Celestials are going to miss sometime so why not make that miss into something that might hit another celestial with that automatic counter attack charm. make them Demetheus their allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safety Among Enemies is a fun trick but keys off a Dodge without PD. It's a fairly safe bet that anything the DB can dodge can also be defended passively by the Solar's ally, so it would be motes and willpower wasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:43:59-08:00","id":417409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417406#post417406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Safety Among Enemies is a fun trick but keys off a Dodge without PD. It's a fairly safe bet that anything the DB can dodge can also be defended passively by the Solar's ally, so it would be motes and willpower wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>aaah but there is where the automatic counter attack comes into play you could just play it of that since it was the db that launched the attack it will trigger against the one that actually preformed the attack that being the celestial this time, it might be borderline cheating i'd guess but i mean let the db's have at least one douche-manouver that the celestials can't just flashlight out of","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T04:50:04-08:00","id":417433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417400#post417400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am confident that Dragon-Bloods of equal Essence and experience can take Solars at a five to one ratio.<br /> <br /> No cheese, no broken artifacts, no &quot;creative&quot; rule interpretations, Akuma bullshit, mutations, merits, whatever. Even in a fight under rules and conditions a sane storyteller would allow, Terrestrials can absolutely win.<br /> <br /> DBs can get a good passive DV+External penalty using the Charms stated above, with no need to spent motes per dodge. This is enough to counter most attacks enhanced with only IAM. In the face of a undodgeable or penalty negating attack, they can group PD using Dragon Vortex or Defend Other PD using Conflagration of Warding. The group's collective stunt recovery will be enough to cover their defence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> By definition, Dragonblooded cannot be &quot;of equal Essence and experience&quot;, nor backgrounds, as the Solar Elders of the time of the Usurpation. So my argument that the Usurpation is a fiat event and that the mechanics of 2/2,5 made DBs a nonentity in the Solar vs Sidereal clash stays.<br /> <br /> I take it you are moving the argument to a 2.5 comparison of 2-5 Essence Solars against similarly powerful but outnumbering them Dragonblooded (and staying away from the less 2.5-y stuff). Well, in 2.5 we did some fights exactly like that and while the DBs provided a challenge in sufficient numbers it was plain that:<br /> <br /> - Solar defenses were much better, high DVs coupled with the likes of Parable Defense, backed up by superior soak and regeneration<br /> - Solar offense was vastly superior between Overdrive and Heroic Presence<br /> - the skewed strategic balance hasn't changed at all...which is, the Solars had the upper hand in choosing engagements and less need for having vulnerable assets spread throughout Creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T05:03:56-08:00","id":417442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417433#post417433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you are moving the argument to a 2.5 comparison of 2-5 Essence Solars against similarly powerful but outnumbering them Dragonblooded (and staying away from the less 2.5-y stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div>I moved nothing, I was never talking about pre-2.5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417433#post417433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Solar defenses were much better, high DVs coupled with the likes of Parable Defense, backed up by superior soak and regeneration<br /> - Solar offense was vastly superior between Overdrive and Heroic Presence<br /> - the skewed strategic balance hasn't changed at all...which is, the Solars had the upper hand in choosing engagements and less need for having vulnerable assets spread throughout Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Solars have many advantages, it's a question of how overwhelming those advantages are. I contend that the power gap between Solars and Terrestrials is not great enough to overcome five to one odds in a sanely managed game. The advantage of group defences like Dragon Vortex, With One Mind and Virtuous Negation Defence is that a group of Terrestrials in close proximity effectively have to be fought as a single entity with combined mote pools and stunt regen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:24:52-08:00","id":417558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417442#post417442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The advantage of group defences like Dragon Vortex, With One Mind and Virtuous Negation Defence is that a group of Terrestrials in close proximity effectively have to be fought as a single entity with combined mote pools and stunt regen.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Solars get immunity to environmental taking care of Dragon Vortex. Virtuous Negation Defense, well, firstly, it fails against undodgeable attacks, on top of my head there are three ways to make an undodgeable attack dodgeable, one in Cobra (banned in 2.5), one in Scroll of the Monk (very not-2.5 splat) and a fey one that's expensive and very complicated to use as DB; secondly it is very hard to beat the successes of Solar attacks with the activation roll, so even against dodgeable Solar attacks you end up as &quot;defending with DV&quot; not with a perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T08:43:32-08:00","id":417574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417558#post417558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How? Solars get immunity to environmental taking care of Dragon Vortex. Virtuous Negation Defense, well, firstly, it fails against undodgeable attacks, on top of my head there are three ways to make an undodgeable attack dodgeable, one in Cobra (banned in 2.5), one in Scroll of the Monk (very not-2.5 splat) and a fey one that's expensive and very complicated to use as DB; secondly it is very hard to beat the successes of Solar attacks with the activation roll, so even against dodgeable Solar attacks you end up as &quot;defending with DV&quot; not with a perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I acknowledged their immunity to the damage of Dragon Vortex, I'm talking about the Shield function of Wrath Directing Gesture that lets it be used as a perfect defence within its radius. Combined with Sculpt it can be reflexively reshaped to PD any attack (including AoE attacks) for 11m.<br /> <br /> Yes, Virtuous Negation Defence fails against Undodgeable attacks, so against such an attack the group would have to fall back on either Dragon Vortex's Shield or, if that is unavailable for some reason, reflexive Defend Other + Conflagration of Warding.<br /> <br /> Yes, the roll is very unlikely to succeed, but it's a superfluous effect. The Charm's main function is to redirect the attack to the defender and apply his DV. As I said, Terrestrial Dodge can contest Solar attack dice pools when you throw in the External penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T09:42:05-08:00","id":417613,"title":"","content":"If you treat the whole scene like a duel between PCs and the dragon-bloods during a mass combat fight, you could stack a group of Dragon Blooded up Dragon Blessed Champion which will let them use the stats from the unit in person combat for a duel. This can more than make up for the discrepancies in dice pools between the two splats. Using the perfect defenses Crumplepunch laid out, you could easily have a group of Dragon-Bloods give the Celestials a run for their money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T12:37:55-08:00","id":417791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417613#post417613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you treat the whole scene like a duel between PCs and the dragon-bloods during a mass combat fight, you could stack a group of Dragon Blooded up Dragon Blessed Champion which will let them use the stats from the unit in person combat for a duel. This can more than make up for the discrepancies in dice pools between the two splats. Using the perfect defenses Crumplepunch laid out, you could easily have a group of Dragon-Bloods give the Celestials a run for their money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was avoiding mass combat because the system as a whole is a terrible mess, but BDC is a very powerful effect, especially with the repurchase. I question whether it would actually be effective on a simlarly specced Solar.<br /> <br /> At higher levels the gap between DB and Solar dice pools (8 vs 10, or 10+stunt and some other cap breakers) is less of an issue than the different design spaces of the two splats. Dragon-Bloods by design have very few and highly situational Unblockable/Undodgeable attacks, no DV halvers, no attack penalty negators, no Overdrives, no tick long perfect defences, no mote expanders, no late stage damage adders and reducers... the list goes on.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods need to ameliorate these weaknesses with numbers, teamwork, and unvarnished but sizeable dice pools. All other things being equal, they can only win if they play to their strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:31:36-08:00","id":417971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/415848-dragon-blooded-defense?p=417791#post417791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was avoiding mass combat because the system as a whole is a terrible mess, but BDC is a very powerful effect, especially with the repurchase. I question whether it would actually be effective on a simlarly specced Solar.<br /> <br /> At higher levels the gap between DB and Solar dice pools (8 vs 10, or 10+stunt and some other cap breakers) is less of an issue than the different design spaces of the two splats. Dragon-Bloods by design have very few and highly situational Unblockable/Undodgeable attacks, no DV halvers, no attack penalty negators, no Overdrives, no tick long perfect defences, no mote expanders, no late stage damage adders and reducers... the list goes on.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods need to ameliorate these weaknesses with numbers, teamwork, and unvarnished but sizeable dice pools. All other things being equal, they can only win if they play to their strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with you that the mass combat system has a lot to be desired, so let me rephrase my suggestion:<br /> <br /> Avoid mass combat by having the battle essentially be decided based on the respective champions and use the raging battle as a backdrop for the fight. However, use the Dragon Blessed Champion charm (among others) to justify giving the DBs substantial bonuses based off the units to which they belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}